c.sha + '|' + …` shadows the module-level `key(c, id)` function. `var body = add(el('div','scroll'), table)` shadows the later module-level `body`, the desk's rail+pane container.\n   - It works today because `hunkView` never calls `key()` or uses the outer `body`. A later edit that does will silently get a string or a wrong element.\n   - Rename them to `foldKey` and `codeEl`. Size: 4 lines.\n\n3. **Duplicated review-class mapping** (`reviews-view`, `reviewStatus`).\n   - `reviewClass(r)` is called twice in a nested ternary to turn `'review-ok'`, `'stale'` or `'review-none'` into `'ok'`, `'warn'` or `'none'`.\n   - Compute `var cls = reviewClass(r)` once, or have `reviewClass` return the semantic name and let the CSS use `.ok`/`.warn`/`.none`. Size: 2 lines.\n   - `entryHead(r, e)` never uses `r`, so drop the parameter.\n   - `reviewShort` and `honestyLabel` both re-derive verdict and state text, and could share a single label function. That is optional.\n\n4. **`keepFocus` lookup** (`desk-layout`).\n   - It loops over every `[data-fid]` element and keeps the last match. That is fine at this size. `app.querySelector('[data-fid=\"' + CSS.escape(fid) + '\"]')` would be shorter and would return the first match.\n   - Size: 3 lines. Low priority.\n\n5. **Dead CSS** (`desk-layout`, `src/html/style.css`).\n   - I did not verify this, but a quick grep for selectors with no producer in `client.js` would be worthwhile. `.filters` and `.main .rows` apply only to range commit panes, and `.overviewrow` and `.railfoot` apply only to single-commit pages. `.review-none` is still used.\n   - Check for leftovers from the rewrite, for example `.entry summary .ehead`, `.chips .chip span` and `.legend + .chips`, and remove any that have no match.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
