 hash up directly. The mapping then sits in one place and `applyHash` becomes about 6 lines.\n   - Size: about 25 lines → 10.\n\n4. **`desk-ui`, `groupPane` and the rail row in `client.js`.** *(read)*\n   - The impact label is built twice, with the same `'(derived)'` logic. `groupPane` builds it inline and `groupRow` uses `impactWord(g)`. Have `groupPane` use `impactWord(g)` too.\n   - `navButtons(pane, c, g)` never uses `c` or `g`. Drop those parameters.\n   - `honestyLabel` re-derives the same state-to-class mapping that `reviewsBlock` builds inline for `r.state/verdict`.\n   - `groupPane` computes `files` and `perFile` by hand, as `fileCount` does for a whole commit.\n   - Size: about 10 lines.\n\n5. **`tests`, the assertions on source text in `attention.test.ts`.** *(read)*\n   - `assert.match(html, /impact' \\+ \\(g\\.impact|' impact' \\+/)` pins an implementation detail of the client source through an alternation regex. It breaks on any refactor, including suggestion 4.\n   - The old assertion had the same weakness. A better check is the storage-blocked Chromium test, which already renders the page. Extend it to assert the rendered impact text, for example `/impact/` in the DOM dump, and drop the source regexes.\n   - Size: 2 lines swapped.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
