3aa0121","ffa9d71b57a39f26","ffb98efc4a87963d","ffcba41ffe46b311","fff4dbc6731f8f2f"],"groups":["608b91febf8bd315","91959db375cf21a0","22b2c25d2c82bf16","54416482276cee4f","57c4ae1e523a5553","1910e9044f6ce19f","4490df430a693b8e","a91fe9ec7da378be","1c233d8479fefc3b","a3bf604b5d4add50","d523a0b50a99feb0","c308bb657ac612ee","f5ad07689903ca40","37d0841f59ea2c70"],"findings":"## Review of the Review desk commit (snapshot 1b7066f)\n\nI found no hard mismatches between the annotations and the code. The main issues are a test gap under a `required` group and a weak rejected-alternative rationale. I did not run the screenshots or the hand-driven browser checks the annotations cite, so those claims are read only.\n\n**Verified**\n- Full suite (`node --test` over `test/*.test.ts`, Chromium at `/usr/bin/chromium`): 171 pass, 0 fail.\n- `tests` group, \"would be unchecked\" claim: I copied the repo to `scratch/mut`, replaced `else refreshNav()` with a no-op in `renderChrome`, and ran the `real browser` test. It fails with `actual: 'true:Previous|false:Next|false:Mark as read and go to next'`. The claim holds, so that test does guard the refreshNav fix.\n\n**Read**\n\n1. **Mismatch: none found.** The `desk-layout`, `read-progress`, `range-order` and `review-order` descriptions match the code. `codeOpen: true` (diff expanded by default), the global `o/e/c` flag, the sha-keyed localStorage marks, and the hottest-first default all match. The `read-progress` storage calls are all wrapped in try/catch, as stated.\n\n2. **Gap under `read-progress` [required], which the annotation already admits.** Nothing tests the read marks themselves: toggling a mark, persisting it across reload, or the progress counter. The only browser test covers Previous/Next and the button label. That is the one feature the author marks as new and required. Suggest adding a Chromium test that clicks a checkbox, reloads, and checks `.row.done` and the `N of M read` text.\n\n3. **Misgrading: `tests` [supporting] is a bundle.** It holds four unrelated tests that each serve one feature: the review order (`reviewOrder` unit test), the rendered attention card, the Previous/Next browser test, and the storage-blocked test. Attaching each test to its owning group would be clearer. As written, `tests` implies the read-marks feature is covered, which it is not. This is a presentation issue, not a defect.\n\n4. **Weak rejected alternative for `review-order` [supporting].** The alternative is rejected as \"Not testable without a browser\". The same suite already drives Chromium (`browse()` in `attention.test.ts`), so that reason does not hold. Computing the order client-side would still be a defensible choice, because `data.ts` gains about 30 lines and the client duplicates the sort. The author should either drop the stated reason or name the duplication cost as the real trade-off. The field is used (`groupPane` crumb and `orderedGroups`), so the group itself is not removable.\n\n5. **Simplification: none needed in the required groups.** The client is large (about 660 lines in one hunk), but the duplication I checked is minor.\n\n6. **Missing risks.**\n   - `browse()` picks a random port in 9300–9899 with no collision check. A busy port would fail intermittently. Minor.\n   - The hash for a single-commit overview is `#overview`, and `applyHash` treats the bare `unannotated` hash as commit 0 only. A range with a commit whose sha7 is `overview` or `unannotated` is not handled. Unlikely, but unguarded.\n   - The `tests` group evidence says the storage-blocked test shows the page works with storage disabled. The test passes `--disable-local-storage` and checks only that the hashed group is selected. It does not verify that storage access actually threw. Read only; I did not check this flag's behaviour in this Chromium build.\n\n7. **Unverified annotation claims** (read only, not run): the CSP \"blocks nothing\" note, the screenshots, the \"three columns inside ary\" risk, and the approximate hunk line ranges for `read-progress` and `range-order`.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
