e group of a commit under \"All\", so Next is disabled and the primary button reads \"Mark as read\". Switch the filter to one that shows more groups after it. Next stays disabled and the label stays wrong. In the opposite case, Next stays enabled but does nothing.\n   - **Related:** `markRead(true); stepTo(1)` still works, because `neighbor` is recomputed when the button is clicked.\n\n2. **Minor (read), `test/gloss.test.ts`, the test \"the page keeps working when local storage is unavailable\".**\n   - **Problem:** `--disable-local-storage` is not a Chromium flag. I believe Chromium ignores unknown flags, and `file://` pages normally have `localStorage`. So the test most likely never exercises the storage-failure path in `readSet` and `setRead`. It passes whether or not those `try/catch` blocks work.\n   - **Fix:** run the test with storage actually blocked, or stub `window.localStorage` to throw.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
