7a39f26","ffb98efc4a87963d","ffcba41ffe46b311","fff4dbc6731f8f2f"],"groups":["20fcf263852de7aa","5c5fd6defa6931fe","ce896c1405297d39","54416482276cee4f","9a3ec511c253b342","1910e9044f6ce19f","4490df430a693b8e","a91fe9ec7da378be","1c233d8479fefc3b","a3bf604b5d4add50","37d0841f59ea2c70"],"findings":"**Mismatches**\n\n1. **`read-progress`, evidence claim is false (read).** The group says \"Previous/Next follow read state in test/attention.test.ts\". That test only toggles the filter segments. `neighbor()` never reads `readSet`, so read marks don't affect Previous/Next at all. The `navBar` comment (\"which neighbours exist depends on them… read marks\") is also wrong. The test title \"follow the filter and read marks\" has the same problem: no read mark is set in the test body.\n\n2. **`tests`, \"stale-navigation fix\" does not exist (read).** The group's \"if removed\" text names a stale-navigation fix. Nothing in the diff or the repo (`grep` for \"stale-nav\", \"stale navig\") implements or tests one. This looks like a leftover from another change.\n\n3. **`desk-layout`, undisclosed behaviour change (read).** The old page defaulted every group's code to collapsed (`setOpen(false)` in `groupCard`). The new client sets `codeOpen: true` (`client.js:19`), so code is expanded by default. The `o`/`e`/`c` keys were also changed from per-card to one global `codeOpen` flag. Neither change is in any group's intent.\n\n4. **`range-order`, evidence is partly unbacked (read).** \"the toggle and j/k commit stepping driven in Chromium\" is not in any test in the hunks. Only the screenshots and the author's own run support it. I could not verify it from the repo.\n\n**Verified**\n\n- The storage-blocked path is really exercised. `chromium --headless=new --disable-local-storage` makes `window.localStorage.setItem` throw `TypeError` (ran it in `scratch/ls`), and without the flag it works. So the `tests` claim that the storage-blocked path is checked holds. The flag is effective.\n\n**Misgraded necessity**\n\n- `tests` is labelled supporting and serves four groups. That is fair. Its `reviewOrder` unit test also checks the ordering rule for `review-order`, and I checked the expected arrays by hand against the rule: they are correct.\n- `desk-layout` is \"required\", and the task is a redesign, so that is fair. But it absorbs the global `codeOpen` change and the read-mark UI wiring (it's in h4 alongside `read-progress`). Those would be better as their own groups.\n\n**Removal candidates**\n\n- The undocumented `codeOpen` default change could be reverted to match the old collapsed default, with little impact on the design. This is my suggestion, not a required fix.\n- The \"Mark as read and go to next\" button label and its `disabled` logic do not depend on read state. Nothing to remove, but the comment should be corrected.\n\n**Simplifications**\n\n- `navBar()` is rebuilt on every `renderChrome`, and `refreshNav` swaps it in. The rebuild is only needed for `disabled` and the label, which depend on the filter and the current position, not on read marks. A comment fix is enough; no code change is needed.\n\n**Missing risks**\n\n- **Read marks outlive a re-gloss (read).** Marks are keyed by commit sha and group id. If the same commit is re-glossed and a group gets the same id but a different intent, it shows as already read. The \"file:// shared origin\" risk is listed; this one is not.\n- **`o`/`e`/`c` keys (read).** They now change state for every group in view. This should be in the risks list as a behaviour change.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
